<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Generation Examples</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure correct LaTeX rendering, we manually process the generated text following Duo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Curly double quotes <code id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">(\u201c, \u201d)</code> replaced with "</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Em dashes/en dashes <code id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">(\u2014, \u2013)</code> replaced with – or -</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Soft hyphens <code id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">(\u00ad)</code> removed (or replaced by a normal hyphen where it makes sense)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any other special characters replaced with a suitable ASCII approximation</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
